Why This Is Asked
- Tests a practical, scalable multi-tenant pattern within a single bucket, emphasizing isolation, encryption, and rapid containment.
- Exercises policy design using S3, KMS, and IAM with MFA, plus a real-time breach response workflow.

Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation via per-tenant S3 prefix and IAM role scope
- SSE-KMS with per-tenant CMKs and encryption context validation
- Containment orchestration using EventBridge, Lambda, and CloudTrail

Code Example
```json
// S3 bucket policy (illustrative)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/Tenant123Role"},
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::tenant-bucket/tenant-123/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"s3:prefix": "tenant-123/"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
```json
// KMS key policy (illustrative)
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/Tenant123Role"},
      "Action": ["kms:Encrypt","kms:Decrypt"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {"kms:EncryptionContext:TenantID": "tenant-123"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the 60-second containment workflow end-to-end? 
- How would you extend this to support new tenants without increasing policy complexity?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-account security design, tenant isolation, and automated containment under breach pressure.

## Key Concepts
- ABAC with per-tenant tags for cross-account access
- MFA-protected, least-privilege AssumeRole using AWS STS
- KMS key policies with rotation and region scoping
- PrivateLink/VPCE to avoid public internet exposure
- Immutable multi-region CloudTrail and Secrets rotation
- Automated breach containment workflow with rapid credential revocation

## Code Example
```javascript
// IAM trust policy snippet showing ABAC + MFA condition
const policy = {
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
    "Resource": "arn:aws:iam::ACCOUNT:role/TenantAccessRole",
    "Condition": {
      "ForAllValues:StringEquals": {
        "aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenantId}"
      },
      "Bool": {"aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent": true},
      "StringEquals": {
        "aws:SourceArn": "arn:aws:execute-api:region:acct:/*",
        "aws:SourceAccount": "111122223333"
      }
    }
  }]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure containment latency and validate it with red-team tests?
- What telemetry would you collect to prove tenant isolation during breach simulations?
